, \"own choosing\" or whatever exact wording step 1 used, and \"no repository lint entry point\" (the fallback note). Keep \"Lint:\". Do not add \"make test\" or \"go test\" to the want list.\n4. Do not touch `.ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt`. It is protected and is currently identical to the starter template. A maintainer may copy the change by hand.\n\n### Test plan\n- `TestEngReviewPromptShape` (internal/roles/eng_review_test.go): the prompt contains the new entry-point and fallback phrases, stays ASCII, under 16 KiB, passes the secret scan and has none of the forbidden strings.\n- `TestEngReviewPromptExamples`: the examples still parse and still contain \"## Checks\" (checks that step 2 broke nothing).\n- `TestEmbeddedEngReviewLoadsAsReviewer`: unchanged, must still pass.\n- Command: `go test ./internal/roles/` then `make lint` (runs go vet and the gofmt check) and `make test`.\n- Failure case: temporarily removing the new sentence makes `TestEngReviewPromptShape` fail (confirm by reasoning or a local edit that is reverted).\n\n### Risk\nLow. Only an embedded prompt text and its test change. No public interface, migration or concurrency. The change is outside merge.protected_paths unless the config lists `internal/roles/`; check .ard/config.yaml before starting. The live .ard/reviewers copy is protected and is deliberately left alone.\n\n### Size\nS. Files: internal/roles/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt, internal/roles/eng_review_test.go.\nEOF\ncat > .ard/160/triage-engineer.md <<'EOF'\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nTightens the starter eng-review prompt so the reviewer runs the repository's own lint entry point (make lint, or what the README or CI names) and falls back to its own tools only when none exists, saying so under Checks. The plan has four steps plus test updates. Size S, risk low.\n\n## Open issues\n- The live reviewer prompt under .ard/reviewers/ is protected and identical to the starter template. It is not part of this plan, so a maintainer may want to apply the same edit by hand.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5831,"cache_read_input_tokens":14925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5831},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c017c92-beaf-4db9-87b1-00113796c80d","uuid":"8e4855b4-cc4f-4c38-89c0-c93b5723ce37","timestamp":"2026-11-23T11:28:25.173Z","request_id":"req_011ChKnEe6umVEzyt6Vabxjq"}
